# Docker build context hygiene.
#
# The `.`-context services (worker, retrieval) copy `packages/`, `apps/`, `plugins/` and the
# dependency manifest. Without this file `COPY apps ./apps` drags in `apps/desktop/node_modules`
# (~355 MB) and `apps/web/node_modules` (~84 MB) — none of which any Python service needs — and
# every code edit re-uploads the whole context. Keep the context to what the Python images
# actually consume.

# VCS / editor / agent state
.git
.gitignore
.claude

# Python caches
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache

# Local virtualenvs (never part of any image; deps come from uv.lock in-image)
.venv
.venv-*
**/.venv
**/.venv-*

# ML training workspaces (datasets, checkpoints, their own venvs). No image consumes
# them; scripts/ is only copied so gen_proto.sh can run. Without this the build
# context balloons past 8 GB.
fine_tuning

# JS deps (the Electron/web clients are built on the host, never inside a Python image)
**/node_modules

# Runtime state and scratch (mounted at run time where needed, never baked in)
data
logs
.output

# Local backup snapshot (a nested working tree, ~36k files) — never part of any image and
# not referenced by any Dockerfile COPY. Excluding it also keeps the build context small.
.delveta-snapshots

# Misc scratch artifacts
*.stackdump
